{#
    One option out of a group, as radio buttons — the `radio` alias.

    WHY NOT A DROPDOWN: the entity asked for this. `radio` and `join` describe the same shape of
    data, one record out of a target table; the only difference is the `#[PIM\Radio]` attribute,
    and its single purpose is to say "show these open, not folded away". Rendering a dropdown here
    would quietly ignore the one instruction the field carries.

    THE GROUP IS ALREADY APPLIED. Both `radio` and `checkbox` accept `PIM\Option`, the shared
    table of every option of every group, and the field states which group is its own — the
    filtering happens in `RelationOptions`, not here.

    THERE IS NO EMPTY RADIO BUTTON. A radio group cannot be unticked once a value is set, so a
    nullable field gets an explicit "nothing chosen" option; without it a value could be changed
    but never removed.
#}
{% include 'widget/_label.html.twig' %}
            <div class="admin-form__radios"{% if field.error %} role="group" aria-invalid="true" aria-describedby="{{ described }}"{% endif %}>
{% if not field.required %}
                <label class="admin-form__label admin-form__label--inline" for="field-{{ field.property }}">
                    <input class="admin-form__radio" type="radio" id="field-{{ field.property }}" name="{{ field.property }}" value=""{% if field.value == '' %} checked{% endif %}>
                    <em>nichts gewählt</em>
                </label>
{% endif %}
{% for option in field.options %}
                <label class="admin-form__label admin-form__label--inline" for="field-{{ field.property }}-{{ loop.index }}">
                    <input class="admin-form__radio" type="radio" id="field-{{ field.property }}-{{ loop.index }}" name="{{ field.property }}" value="{{ option.value }}"{% if option.value == field.value %} checked{% endif %}{% if field.required and loop.first %} required{% endif %}>
                    {{ option.label }}
                </label>
{% endfor %}
            </div>
